# Files copied into a newly created agent worktree. Gitignore syntax; a file is copied only
# when it matches a pattern here AND is gitignored, so tracked content is never duplicated.

# Accumulated Claude Code permission grants (~12 KB of them). A worktree is a fresh checkout,
# so without this a session there starts with none and re-prompts for things already approved
# in the main checkout: git add/commit, python3 -, reads of the sibling ../a12-kernel source.
# Ignored per-developer via a global gitignore rather than this repo's, so if you have no such
# file nothing is copied and this line is inert.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Deliberately NOT copied, so nobody adds them later thinking it was an oversight:
#   .claude/scheduled_tasks.lock   a lock — a stale one copied into a fresh worktree is worse
#                                  than none
#   .claude/worktrees/             the worktree root itself; recursive
#   .uv-cache/ .uv-tools/          derived caches, regenerated on demand
#   build/ .gradle/ .kotlin/       derived output; the isolated GRADLE_USER_HOME lives OUTSIDE
#                                  the repo (../.gradle-isolated) and is already shared
#   corpus/**/settings.yaml        written by A12 Tools when a folder is opened as a workspace.
#                                  Copy it only if you routinely open corpus models from inside
#                                  a worktree — the tool recreates it, and a copied one carries
#                                  stale workspace state.
